  "question": {
    "text": "If $a \\neq 0$ and the line $2 b x+3 c y+4 d=0$ passes through the points of intersection of the parabolas $y^2=4 a x$ and $x^2=4 a y$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jDCvD",
      "text": "\n$d^2+(2 b+3 c)^2=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9ZGrt",
      "text": "\n$d^2+(3 b+2 c)^2=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DsbTo",
      "text": "\n$d^2+(2 b-3 c)^2=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3groO",
      "text": "\n$d^2+(3 b-2 c)^2=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Points of intersection of given parabolas are $(0,0)$ and $(4 a, 4 a)$ $\\Rightarrow$ equation of line passing through these points is $y=x$ On comparing this line with the given line $2 b x+3 c y+4 d=0$, we get $d=0$ and $2 b+3 c=0 \\Rightarrow(2 b+3 c)^2+d^2=0$",
    "image": null
  },
